# Game files stay out of the repository

The repository contains no game archives, decompilation, or quoted dialogue in notes. The engine does not read the executable. Fonts come from the user's `Resource.pak`. Menu captions, verb labels, slot labels, the three refusal captions, and the numeric tables live in the modules that use them.

Do not add to git:

- game archives (`*.pak`, `*.phk`, `*.ph2`), the executable (`*.exe`), saves (`*.sav`, `*.avx`), or a ZIP of the game
- screenshots, cover art, and the logo
- a decompilation or a binary-analysis project
- a quoted line, a script body, or a complete game configuration file (scene, dialogue, variable table)

Do not paste a spoken line, a script body, or a complete configuration into notes or into a module that does not own that text. A test of other behavior uses a short, invented label. A note describes the effect, without the wording of the line.

```ts
// Wrong: a caption copied into a random module, or a quoted spoken line.
expect(texts.load).toBe("<menu caption copied into this test>");

// Right: short invented label. State the outcome without quoting the line.
expect(texts.load).toBe("Open slot");
```

Pre-publication checklist: `docs/LEGAL.md`.
